From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:39:48 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: vfe: Toggle the frame drop period once
 per update

The gen1 VFE restarts an output's frame drop pattern on the frame where
a new frame drop period takes effect, which is why
vfe_output_frame_drop() toggles the period between two values on each
call. Called twice before the hardware takes the registers, it puts the
old period back: the period the hardware sees doesn't change, and the
pattern carries on from where it was.

That happens when a frame completes with no buffer queued after it, and
a buffer is queued before the next frame starts:
vfe_buf_update_wm_on_last() switches the output to single buffer mode
and vfe_buf_update_wm_on_new() back to continuous mode, each with a
toggle. With the two frames of the continuous pattern used up, the VFE
then drops frames until the period ends, 31 frames or a second of video
at 30 fps. The libcamera simple pipeline, which keeps few buffers
queued, runs into it every few seconds with a 3840x2160 software ISP
stream on msm8996.

Toggle the period only once until the register update done interrupt
shows the hardware took it.

Tested on a Samsung Galaxy Tab S3 (msm8996), with 12 s recordings from
the IMX258 at 4208x2368 over RDI0, in which the VFE ran down to its
last buffer 9 to 87 times: without the fix about two thirds of them
stopped for 1028 ms at least once, with it five had no gap between raw
frames longer than 91 ms.

Fixes: 4c98a5f57f90 ("media: camss: Add VFE files")
Signed-off-by: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe-gen1.c   | 16 +++++++++++++---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.h    |  1 +
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe-gen1.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe-gen1.c
index d84a375e33..a9e41f88e4 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe-gen1.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe-gen1.c
@@ -152,9 +152,17 @@ static void vfe_output_frame_drop(struct vfe_device *vfe,
 	u8 drop_period;
 	unsigned int i;
 
-	/* We need to toggle update period to be valid on next frame */
-	output->drop_update_idx++;
-	output->drop_update_idx %= VFE_FRAME_DROP_UPDATES;
+	/*
+	 * We need to toggle update period to be valid on next frame. Toggle
+	 * it once per register update: toggled again before the hardware
+	 * takes it, the period would not change and the pattern would not
+	 * restart, which drops frames until the current period ends.
+	 */
+	if (!output->gen1.drop_update_pending) {
+		output->drop_update_idx++;
+		output->drop_update_idx %= VFE_FRAME_DROP_UPDATES;
+		output->gen1.drop_update_pending = 1;
+	}
 	drop_period = VFE_FRAME_DROP_VAL + output->drop_update_idx;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < output->wm_num; i++) {
@@ -320,6 +328,7 @@ static int vfe_get_output(struct vfe_line *line)
 	}
 
 	output->drop_update_idx = 0;
+	output->gen1.drop_update_pending = 0;
 
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&vfe->output_lock, flags);
 
@@ -549,6 +558,7 @@ static void vfe_isr_reg_update(struct vfe_device *vfe, enum vfe_line_id line_id)
 	vfe->res->hw_ops->reg_update_clear(vfe, line_id);
 
 	output = &line->output;
+	output->gen1.drop_update_pending = 0;
 
 	if (output->wait_reg_update) {
 		output->wait_reg_update = 0;
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.h b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.h
index a2188a81bc..d5b79baa01 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.h
@@ -70,6 +70,7 @@ struct vfe_output {
 		struct {
 			int active_buf;
 			int wait_sof;
+			int drop_update_pending;
 		} gen1;
 		struct {
 			int active_num;
